          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>From 15 August 2006 to 15 August 2011 is five years. This includes one leap year, 2008. So total extra days are four normal years and one leap year, which gives five extra days.</p><p>From 15 August 2011 to 19 February 2012 is 189 days. Dividing by seven gives remainder zero, so no extra shift.</p><p>Starting from Tuesday, adding five days leads to Sunday.</p><p>Correct answer is Sunday.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04f0b1d98f39-q12",
      "number": 12,
      "question": "Question 12",
      "questionHtml": "",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "C",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "D",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        }
      ],
      "correctAnswer": "D",
      "solution": "<p>From 5 August 2005 to 5 August 2010 is 5 years.</p><p>In these 5 years, leap years are 2008 only, so extra 1 day.</p><p>Total extra days from years = 5 plus 1 = 6 days.</p><p>Now count days from 5 August 2010 to 17 April 2011:</p><p>August to April adds up to 255 days, which is 36 weeks and 3 days.</p><p>So total extra days = 6 plus 3 = 9 days</p><p>9 days ahead of Friday is Sunday.</p>",
      "images": [],
      "subject": null,
      "topic": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    {
      "id": "04f0b1d98f39-q13",
      "number": 13,
      "question": "Question 13",
      "questionHtml": "",
      "options": [
        {
          "id": "A",
          "text": "",
          "html": ""
        },
        {
          "id": "B",
          "text": "",
